---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Page from "../components/ui/Page.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/ui/PageHero.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/ui/Eyebrow.astro";
import Heading from "../components/ui/Heading.astro";
import Lead from "../components/ui/Lead.astro";
import Text from "../components/ui/Text.astro";
import Highlight from "../components/ui/Highlight.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import "../styles/pages/privacy.css";

import {
  TALLY_CONTACT_URL,
  USE_CONTACT_MODAL,
} from "../config/integrations.js";
const UPDATED = "5 November 2026";
const GA_ID = "G-2BF7VRSXYF";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy & cookies | Noesis Vision"
  description="Which cookies the Noesis Vision website uses, what Google Analytics records with your consent, and how to change your choice."
>
  <Page>
    <Nav current="privacy" />

    <main id="main">
      <PageHero class="privacy-hero">
        <Eyebrow>Privacy</Eyebrow>
        <Heading as="h1" size="lg" class="privacy-title">
          Privacy &amp; cookies
        </Heading>
        <Lead class="privacy-lead">
          The short version: we use <Highlight>Google Analytics</Highlight> only
          if you allow it, and we never show ads.
        </Lead>
      </PageHero>

      <div class="privacy-body">
        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Cookies</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            We ask before setting any cookie that isn't needed for the site to
            work. The consent banner is provided by CookieYes, which also keeps
            a record of your choice so we can show that consent was given.
          </Text>
          <ul class="privacy-list">
            <li>
              <code class="code-inline">cookieyes-consent</code>: remembers your
              choice. Always set, because without it we would have to ask on
              every page.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code class="code-inline">_ga</code> and{" "}
              <code class="code-inline">_ga_{GA_ID.slice(2)}</code>: Google
              Analytics, only if you accept analytics. They tell visits apart so
              we can count them, and last about 13 months.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="privacy-actions">
            <Button variant="outline" size="lg" data-consent-settings>
              Cookie settings
            </Button>
            <p class="privacy-note" data-consent-unavailable hidden>
              The cookie settings couldn't be opened, probably because a content
              blocker stops the consent banner. With it, no analytics cookies
              are set.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Analytics</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            If you accept analytics, Google Analytics 4 records which pages you
            visit and which main buttons you use, such as "Request Contact",
            along with the device, browser and approximate location Google
            derives from the request. We use it only to understand how the site
            is used. Nothing from Google loads until you accept, and you can
            withdraw at any time with Cookie settings above.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Storage in your browser</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            One small, temporary entry helps navigation work. When you follow a
            link from another page to a section of the homepage (such as
            Founders), your browser briefly remembers which section to scroll
            to. It is kept in <code class="code-inline">sessionStorage</code>{" "}
            under the key <code class="code-inline">noesis-scroll-target</code>{" "}
            and is deleted on the next page load. It never leaves your device
            and holds no personal information.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Forms</h2>
          {USE_CONTACT_MODAL && (
            <Text size="lg">
              The contact form sends what you type into it (name, email, company
              and message) to Web3Forms, a form service that forwards it to us
              by email. We use it to reply to your request.
            </Text>
          )}
          <Text size="lg">
            The newsletter form sends your email address to MailerLite, the
            service we use to manage the subscriber list and send the
            newsletter. You can unsubscribe at any time with the link in every
            email.
          </Text>
          <Text size="lg">
            Nothing you type is sent until you press the button. When you open
            the newsletter form, your browser makes one empty request to
            MailerLite to check that signups aren't blocked on your device. It
            carries no form data, only what every web request includes, such as
            your IP address.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Links to other sites</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            Some links take you to services run by others, for example Tally (
            {USE_CONTACT_MODAL ? "beta sign-up" : "contact and beta forms"}),
            Substack (newsletter), YouTube, LinkedIn, GitHub, Discord and our
            documentation on GitHub Pages. Once you are on those sites, their
            own privacy and cookie policies apply.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Changes</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            If we add any other cookies, trackers or services that receive your
            data, we will update this page first.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-block">
          <h2 class="privacy-heading">Who we are</h2>
          <Text size="lg">
            This website is run by Noesis Vision Sp.&nbsp;z&nbsp;o.o. If you
            have questions,
            {USE_CONTACT_MODAL ? (
              <a href="#contact" data-open="contact">
                get in touch
              </a>
            ) : (
              <a href={TALLY_CONTACT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                get in touch
              </a>
            )}{" "}
            with us through our contact form.
          </Text>
        </section>

        <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </Page>
  <script>
    import "../scripts/nav.js";

    // "Cookie settings": reopen the CookieYes banner. If CookieYes never loaded (blocked,
    // or a dev/preview build without it), say so instead of doing nothing.
    const button = document.querySelector("[data-consent-settings]");
    const note = document.querySelector("[data-consent-unavailable]");
    button?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (typeof window.revisitCkyConsent === "function")
        window.revisitCkyConsent();
      else if (note) note.hidden = false;
    });
  </script>
</Base>
